      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.21902411965762866,
        "y0": 0.6644070958298345,
        "x1": 0.8018829858603598,
        "y1": 0.6773632711016367
      },
      "text": "The stability of maximizing measures for a penalty function of a subshift",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19885607807576156,
        "y0": 0.6797992633810519,
        "x1": 0.6308934828814339,
        "y1": 0.692755438652854
      },
      "text": "of finite type was established by Gonschorowski et al.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6401340003774948,
        "y0": 0.6797992633810519,
        "x1": 0.7125744731486344,
        "y1": 0.692755438652854
      },
      "text": "[GQS21].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7218149906446953,
        "y0": 0.6797991546485882,
        "x1": 0.8014793588333771,
        "y1": 0.6927553299203905
      },
      "text": "A penalty",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": null,
      "text": "arXiv:2503.06958v2  [math.DS]  11 Mar 2025",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19885710387670694,
        "y0": 0.6951908329037193,
        "x1": 0.801478589482668,
        "y1": 0.7081470081755215
      },
      "text": "function is defined on the forbidden set of a subshift of finite type, assigning a",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19885710387670694,
        "y0": 0.7105830004549366,
        "x1": 0.8014808975347951,
        "y1": 0.7235391757267389
      },
      "text": "value of 0 to admissible local configurations near the origin and −1 otherwise",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1988571551667542,
        "y0": 0.7259751680061539,
        "x1": 0.8014788972229517,
        "y1": 0.7389313432779561
      },
      "text": "(see §2 for more details). It is straightforward to see that every maximizing",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1988570012966124,
        "y0": 0.741366846261285,
        "x1": 0.8016822109703257,
        "y1": 0.7543230215330872
      },
      "text": "measure of a penalty function is supported on the given subshift of finite",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1988570012966124,
        "y0": 0.7567590138125023,
        "x1": 0.8018821395745799,
        "y1": 0.7697151890843045
      },
      "text": "type. In the one-dimensional case, maximizing measures remain supported",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1988570012966124,
        "y0": 0.7721506920676333,
        "x1": 0.8016802619485294,
        "y1": 0.7851068673394355
      },
      "text": "on the given subshift under Lipschitz perturbations for any subshift of finite",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1988570012966124,
        "y0": 0.7874003294811113,
        "x1": 0.8016788771172532,
        "y1": 0.8003565047529134
      },
      "text": "type. However, in the two-dimensional case, there exists a subshift of finite",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1988570012966124,
        "y0": 0.8027920077362423,
        "x1": 0.4374455299698004,
        "y1": 0.8157481830080444
      },
      "text": "type where this stability fails.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.21902506852350315,
        "y0": 0.8181841752874597,
        "x1": 0.8017356551995798,
        "y1": 0.8311403505592618
      },
      "text": "In [GQS21], the authors highlight the difference between one and two di-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19885714234424237,
        "y0": 0.833576143495827,
        "x1": 0.8014794485909599,
        "y1": 0.8465323187676291
      },
      "text": "mensions, demonstrating that instability arises in a penalty function of the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1988571551667542,
        "y0": 0.8489678308119967,
        "x1": 0.8016801593684348,
        "y1": 0.8619240060837988
      },
      "text": "Robinson tiling, which is a two-dimensional subshift of finite type with no",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.21902522239364497,
        "y0": 0.8763579835234798,
        "x1": 0.4941183651194853,
        "y1": 0.8870068910286149
      },
      "text": "2010 Mathematics Subject Classification.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5019847196691176,
        "y0": 0.8763579835234798,
        "x1": 0.7115306181066177,
        "y1": 0.8870068910286149
      },
      "text": "Primary 37B51, 37B10, 37B25.",
      "html": null,
